From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: the desktop selects many icons and drags them

David: the icons need to be draggable, and a drag should select many icons.
The desktop selected one icon at a time and nothing could be dragged. Now,
as Windows' desktop:

- a press on the empty desktop and a drag draws a rubber band (translucent,
  over the icons) that selects the icons it touches; Ctrl+click adds or takes
  out an icon, Shift+click selects from the last icon clicked, Ctrl+A all;
- an icon dragged (with the other selected icons) moves on the desktop's
  grid, a picture of the icons following the mouse; the places are kept
  (HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Desktop\IconPositions, as Windows keeps them
  with Auto arrange off) and Sort by lines the icons up again;
- the drag is OLE's, with the shell's data object for the files
  (IShellFolder::GetUIObjectOf): dropped on a folder icon (drawn as the
  target), the Recycle Bin or a File Explorer window, the files move or copy
  there by the target's own rule;
- the desktop is a drop target: files dropped from File Explorer go into the
  Desktop folder, placed where they were dropped;
- the icon menu, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Delete and Enter act on every selected icon
  (from the user's and the public Desktop together: Delete goes folder by
  folder, the rest through the namespace root).

SG_DESKTOP_DUMP's first line adds selcount=, sel= (the selected icons),
band=1 while a band is drawn and drop= (the icon a drag is over).

Gate: make test-drag.
